<Resource id="override_field" type="field_map" name="V5RC Override 2026-2027">
    <!--
    V5RC Override 2026-2027 nominal field geometry.

    Field frame, viewed from the Audience View:
      origin        = inside bottom-left of the 3566.4 mm nominal field
      +x            = right
      +y            = toward the top / 0-degree wall in the VEX drawing
      +z            = up
      planar angle  = counterclockwise from +x

    Landmark origins are the plan-view centers of the goals projected onto
    the field floor. Every landmark frame is aligned with the field frame,
    so every NominalPose heading is zero. Tag surface frames use +x as the
    outward surface normal and +z as the decoded printed top.

    Geometry is derived from the official 2026-04-26 STEP and remains
    provisional until checked against physical field elements. The
    tagCircle21h7 detection size is the detector-corner edge, not the
    carrier plate or outer printed graphic.

    Dimensions, Feature and Visual elements are display data for the
    inspection viewer, from Game Manual v2.0 Appendix A and the CAD parse
    described in docs/field_assets.md. Estimation never reads them; a
    wrong value there moves a picture, not an estimate.
    -->

    <!--
    Perimeter: 276-8242 portable field perimeter, manual v2.0 sheet A13
    (140.40 in [3566.4 mm] inside wall to wall, 11.54 in [293 mm] wall
    height, 2.00 in [50.8 mm] wall thickness). The metal perimeter
    278-1501 on sheet A14 is 3568.7 mm inside with 292.1 mm walls. Tile
    pitch is inside/6; the CAD tile part 276-6904-001 is a 618.1 mm
    interlocking square, so the part size is not the pitch.
    -->
    <Dimensions
        inside_x_m="3.5664"
        inside_y_m="3.5664"
        wall_height_m="0.293"
        wall_thickness_m="0.0508"
        tile_m="0.5944"
        source="V5RC Override Game Manual v2.0 Appendix A sheets A10 and A13; CAD 276-9250-000 (2026-04-26)"
        revision="manual v2.0 (2026-09-03); CAD zip Last-Modified 2026-04-27"
        units_note="meters here; the manual gives inches [mm]; tile pitch = inside/6, the CAD tile part is 618.1 mm interlocking"/>

